    Solve the first stage of the joint shared and own groups
    
    The trusted planner now adds the main-only position bound on the way up and
    solves the shared and own groups together: each round recomputes the random
    tails from the current position counts, sizes the groups under the joint draw
    counts, and stops when no count grows. A settled solution must have every
    sized group holding its rounds at the target; otherwise the configuration is
    reported with its failing point. Groups can now be sized without mask rows,
    which the main-only bound needs; the existing two-stage path keeps its plan
    behavior. Unit tests cover a converged first stage, a capacity failure and a
    zero batch.
    
    This is the first-stage fixed point only; the capacity mapping and the
    whole-chain round budget remain the next steps.

